  <!-- Part 2 -->
  <div class=3D"part-heading" id=3D"part2">
    <span class=3D"part-num">Part 02</span>
    <h2>The Infrastructure Problem: Why Single-VM RAG Fails</h2>
  </div>

  <p>The initial implementation ran every component as a Docker container o=
n a single GCP VM. Each component had a hard ceiling =E2=80=94 and when one=
 failed, it took down the entire system for every tenant simultaneously.</p=
>

  <div class=3D"table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>What Breaks</th><th>Why</th></tr></t=
head>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>ChromaDB</td><td>Slows then crashes</td><td>In-memory vecto=
r store has no persistence or sharding. At 100K+ documents it exhausts RAM<=
/td></tr>
        <tr><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>Connection limit hit</td><td>A container=
 can handle ~100 connections. Enterprise with 50 concurrent users =C3=97 co=
nnection pools =3D exceeded</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Redis</td><td>OOM eviction</td><td>Container has fixed memo=
ry. Redis starts evicting cache entries, causing rate limit state to disapp=
ear</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FastAPI</td><td>~50 concurrent requests</td><td>Single cont=
ainer cannot scale horizontally. CPU-bound under load</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Streamlit</td><td>~20 concurrent users</td><td>Each user ge=
ts their own Python process =E2=80=94 not suitable for enterprise multi-use=
r</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Groq</td><td>Rate limited</td><td>Free tier has strict toke=
ns/min cap =E2=80=94 fails under real enterprise query volume</td></tr>
        <tr><td>No monitoring</td><td>Silent failures</td><td>No visibility=
 into which queries fail, why answers are wrong, or what the cost is</td></=
tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class=3D"callout callout-note">
    <span class=3D"callout-badge">=E2=9A=A0 Core Problem</span>
    <p>When one component fails on a single VM, it takes down the entire sy=
stem for every enterprise tenant simultaneously. There is no isolation, no =
scaling, no failover.</p>
  </div>

