  <h3>Feature 3: Per-Tenant Isolation at the Vector DB Layer</h3>

  <p>In a multi-tenant RAG system, the most critical isolation requirement =
is that Tenant A's documents never appear in Tenant B's query results. Pine=
cone implements this via <strong>namespaces</strong>: every <code style=3D"=
font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:0.85em">retrieve()</code> =
call passes <code style=3D"font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size=
:0.85em">namespace=3Dtenant_id</code>, and Pinecone enforces isolation at t=
he query level.</p>

  <div class=3D"callout callout-note">
    <span class=3D"callout-badge">=E2=9A=99 Architecture Detail</span>
    <p>Strict isolation without running separate vector databases per tenan=
t. All tenants share the same managed Pinecone infrastructure, but their da=
ta is completely separated. Adding a new tenant requires no infrastructure =
changes =E2=80=94 just use a new namespace string.</p>
  </div>

